James inquired about representing a model combination process in mathematical form, specifically focusing on constructing an empirical distribution function. I provided a structured approach, defining key variables related to the models' distributions and their root-mean-squared-errors (RMSE). First, we calculated weights as inverses of RMSE values, normalized these to form selection probabilities, and detailed how to generate samples from the models based on those probabilities. Finally, I outlined the construction of the empirical distribution function using the samples generated. This exchange emphasized combining models effectively to approximate a mixture distribution through weighted sampling.
